{"seq":24,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T08:24:55.491Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"3bb7d2f4b8c0ff96233bc5898621db515c2e8c7483dc92a732c902bc5cc8afca","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"Here's what I found for Marrow Fieldworks:\n\n- #4409: Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026). Recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, 06:00 flatbed intake).\n- #4412: same Moss note. Driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n- PD-5302: #central-random, Hollis on 14 Oct. A follow-up from this week, no action needed.\n\nOne caveat on the first two: the note lists them under the Marrow Fieldworks handoff (5 Jan) but calls it \"Pree's dealer account\" rather than using the name.\n\nThings I left out on purpose:\n- #8841 (#central-random, Tobias on 13 Oct): Door 2 double-booking at the West yard, filed under \"Tobias's dealer account\". The account isn't named. If Fieldworks moved to Tobias in that January handoff, this could be one too, so worth checking with him.\n- FR-882 (same Moss note) and PD-4821 (#central-team, June) are for Marrow Agrisupply, not Fieldworks.\n\nNothing else this week mentions a Fieldworks ticket in the channels you're in, and there are no Marrow Fieldworks account or ticket files I can see."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
