{"seq":26,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T08:25:05.615Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"7ada2c82bd031d25ff32085643cd50767abfe98d7713083161816518033198d0","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"Pree, I found three ticket numbers for Marrow Fieldworks and sent you the list in our DM:\n\n- #4409: from Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026). It's a timeout that keeps coming back on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard, at Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake.\n- #4412: from the same Moss note. A driver text-message prompt glitches when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n- PD-5302: from #central-random. Hollis posted it on 14 Oct as a follow-up from this week, with no action needed.\n\nOne caveat: Moss's note doesn't name the account for #4409 and #4412. It lists them under the Marrow Fieldworks handoff on 5 Jan but calls it \"Pree's dealer account.\"\n\nTickets I left out:\n- #8841 (#central-random, Tobias, 13 Oct): West yard Door 2 is double-booking. Tobias filed it under \"Tobias's dealer account\" without naming the account. If Fieldworks moved to Tobias in the January handoff, this could be a Fieldworks ticket too, so it's worth asking him.\n- FR-882 (the same Moss note) and PD-4821 (#central-team, Hollis, 9 June) are both Marrow Agrisupply, not Fieldworks.\n\nMy first message said PD-4821 came from \"June\". I sent a follow-up making clear I meant the month, 9 June, and that Hollis posted it.\n\nI only looked in the channels you're in and the files anyone can open. I found no other Fieldworks ticket numbers from this week, and no Marrow Fieldworks account or ticket files that I can see."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1792159200.000129"}}
